ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"851183dd14707ed6727996798119a33e51466e6f3f4f446aeee530cb4c12f5cd","event_uuid":"bec7ff31-bab6-4e59-9658-a3659acea245","position":{"commit_sha":"4b84a409a137b5b3b7525000a53c631cb9014eb5","position":"1786559771939709001-bec7ff31-bab6-4e59-9658-a3659acea245"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"463c6b0f362b2cbfbf8e6054f2ad63b114b0ed0b63ce071796bebe91925a2e32","event_uuid":"d109b200-d580-4442-8b79-eeefe47e9d22","position":{"commit_sha":"4b84a409a137b5b3b7525000a53c631cb9014eb5","position":"1786559773154853001-d109b200-d580-4442-8b79-eeefe47e9d22"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e2bf8653fcea4cda602f8009759576c35c0f0a23251d72dfdb08768ccc79d2f7","event_uuid":"2c0531a6-311c-462e-9d43-ec7c247b654b","position":{"commit_sha":"973617a8a4e1ad96f0c64e8aa67e90a627035ff1","position":"1786560886133597735-2c0531a6-311c-462e-9d43-ec7c247b654b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-227_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","comments":[],"created_at":1786163034106637001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"52b2f61d-c892-4ed0-9fb5-8e96326386d3","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"2bc9-75aa-a08a-478a"},{"link_uuid":"2c0531a6-311c-462e-9d43-ec7c247b654b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9dcf-ffce-08db-40de"}],"description":"## Context\n\nGerrit review of change 1536 confirmed the new locked commit-and-push entrypoint safely fails\nclosed when local lock-artifact exclusion cannot be installed, and that the pre-lock update may\nappend harmless duplicate exclude lines under concurrent first use. Preserve the shipped\ncompatibility contract while tightening the local metadata update and its direct failure\noracles.\n\n## Current state (verified against origin/main cc69cc1179)\n\n`_ignore_lock_artifacts` (src/rebar/_store/push.py:606-629) resolves `info/exclude`, reads it,\ncomputes the missing patterns, and appends them with a buffered `open(..., \"a\")` that can issue\nTWO writes (a leading newline, then the patterns). It is called at push.py:651, BEFORE the write\nlock is taken — deliberately, since the exclusion must exist before anything can stage — so two\nfirst-time callers genuinely race here.\n\nTwo racing buffered appends can interleave at the byte level and tear a pattern into a corrupt\nhalf-line (e.g. `.ticket-write.lo`), which would silently stop excluding the lock artifact. That\nis the real hazard; a duplicated WHOLE line is not.\n\nTest coverage gaps in tests/unit/test_commit_and_push_tickets_branch_heldout.py (331 lines): the\nexisting tests cover `git add` / `git commit` failure (line 190), lock failure (228), the\nrecovery guard (156), push-only (259) and the CLI (277). Nothing directly covers the\nexclusion-write failure gate (push.py:651-655), the `git status` failure gate (push.py:673-678),\nor proves that lock artifacts stay out of a real commit.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. push.py `_ignore_lock_artifacts`: hoist the pattern tuple to a module constant and replace the\n   buffered two-write append with a SINGLE `os.write` to an `O_WRONLY|O_APPEND` descriptor. POSIX\n   applies that one write at end-of-file atomically, so a racing pair can no longer tear a\n   pattern. Document in the docstring that a duplicated whole line remains possible and is the\n   deliberate disposition — git applies a repeated exclude pattern identically, so the file stays\n   semantically idempotent, and removing the duplicate would require a lock this function must\n   not take (it runs before the write lock and stays outside the recovery guard, both unchanged).\n   Do not change the read-failure disposition (`OSError` still returns False / fails closed).\n   Scope note: single-write `O_APPEND` atomicity is a POSIX guarantee, which matches this\n   project's declared support surface — pyproject.toml classifies it `Operating System :: POSIX`\n   and `MacOS :: MacOS X` (no Windows classifier) and every CI job runs on `ubuntu-latest`. The\n   docstring states that scope rather than implying a universal guarantee.\n2. Tests, added to the held-out file:\n   - exclusion-write failure, strict and default: force `_ignore_lock_artifacts` to fail and\n     assert strict raises `PushDeliveryError` with reason `stage-failed` while default logs a\n     warning and returns; the dirty content is retained and a clean retry commits and delivers.\n   - `git status` failure, strict and default: same split, same retained-content + clean-retry\n     oracle, reaching the push.py:673-678 branch specifically.\n   - real legacy-tracker commit: with both lock artifacts present on disk, commit and assert via\n     `git ls-tree -r` that neither `.ticket-write.lock` nor anything under `.ticket-write.lock.d/`\n     entered the committed tree, and that a clean retry succeeds.\n   - concurrent first use: run the exclude update from several workers against one fresh tracker\n     and assert every line of `info/exclude` is a whole, intact pattern (no torn line) and both\n     patterns are present.\n3. Keep push.py within the 800-line module-size gate — it is at 789 today, so the change must be\n   close to net-neutral.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/test_commit_and_push_tickets_branch_heldout.py -q` (the held-out commit-and-push suite).\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit -k \"push\" -q` (the push-only compatibility suites).\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint` and `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck`.\n- `awk 'END{print NR}' src/rebar/_store/push.py` stays at or below the 800 in `.github/module-size-limit.txt`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 — Concurrent first use cannot corrupt local exclude metadata on the supported POSIX platforms; duplicate-line disposition is documented or eliminated. Proved by the concurrent-first-use test asserting no torn line.\n- [ ] AC2 — Strict and default exclusion/status failures are directly covered with observable typed-error or warning/return outcomes. Proved by the four new failure tests (`stage-failed` reason vs caplog warning + return).\n- [ ] AC3 — A real legacy tracker commit proves lock artifacts are absent from the resulting commit and a clean retry succeeds. Proved by the `git ls-tree -r` oracle over the committed tree.\n- [ ] AC4 — Existing push-only and commit-and-push compatibility suites remain green, checked by the pytest commands above; `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass and push.py stays within the module-size gate.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/push.py","reason":"harden local lock-artifact exclude update without changing delivery contracts"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_commit_and_push_tickets_branch_heldout.py","reason":"direct exclusion/status failure and committed-artifact oracles"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","9dcf-ffce-08db-40de"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"bec7ff31-bab6-4e59-9658-a3659acea245","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["store","concurrency","testing"],"ticket_id":"210c-b695-f0a3-46e4","ticket_type":"task","title":"Harden lock-artifact exclusion metadata and failure coverage","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["6345b179-851c-4277-879a-d77f9ef5b4d6","4584da33-20a8-420c-9f70-5b0c6f23ae4f","52b2f61d-c892-4ed0-9fb5-8e96326386d3","227e71b6-58dd-4b11-a255-5e1b59b2d3b7","01b7acab-bc85-4317-a948-5e65fc49f4a0","585e9db7-f850-4367-adfb-f1ab4c8edde0","777283b6-0e26-4c84-b21f-7b2af112ab02","bec7ff31-bab6-4e59-9658-a3659acea245","d109b200-d580-4442-8b79-eeefe47e9d22","2c0531a6-311c-462e-9d43-ec7c247b654b"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786560886133597736,"uuid":"6ff4e7d6-912b-4eec-8b21-1c116437727c"}